Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), golang-go (>= 2:1.22~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/wisp-boot/wisp

Package: wisp
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dmsetup, kbd, console-setup
Provides: linux-initramfs-tool
Conflicts: initramfs-tools, dracut
Description: reproducible pure-Go initramfs for encrypted root file systems
 wisp builds an initramfs whose bytes are a pure function of a declared
 manifest and the kernel package: same inputs, same bytes, so its hash can
 be predicted on another machine. The initramfs holds one static Go binary
 as /init, which finds the hardware without udev, opens LUKS2 without
 cryptsetup, activates a linear logical volume without lvm2, and switches
 to the real root. Nothing is scanned from the running machine at build
 time and nothing is parsed before it is measured at boot time.
 .
 wisp replaces initramfs-tools: it writes /boot/initrd.img-<version>, is
 called by the kernel hooks, and answers to update-initramfs.
